From 267e55982fee643f349e084f31f56bf44fcb7801 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Degenhardt <bmd@bmdhacks.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:26:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tu: restore the a7xx RB clear/buffer/CCU registers when
 switching back into a command buffer

On an Adreno 722 under KGSL, the CP switches to a higher priority context
(SurfaceFlinger's GLES composition, in the app) inside the bins of a GMEM
render pass, not at the end of a bin, so the bin restore preamble that
rewrites RB_CLEAR_TARGET, RB_BUFFER_CNTL and RB_CCU_CACHE_CNTL never runs, and
the CP's own restore leaves them as the other context set them. With
RB_CLEAR_TARGET in sysmem mode, the GMEM clears in the rest of the pass go to
the attachment in memory instead of the tile, and the pass comes out with its
earlier bins black or stale and only its last bin correct.

Every write of the three registers on a7xx now also writes the value to
tu6_global, and a switch-back amble (CP_SET_AMBLE PREAMBLE_AMBLE_TYPE, which
the CP runs on every switch back into a command buffer) writes them back.
Command buffers that track preemption latency get the restore in front of
their own switch-back amble. Reading the registers in a switch-away amble
instead does not work on the Adreno 722: CP_REG_TO_MEM returns 0 for all
three there.

Measured on a Retroid Pocket Duo with a Burnout 3 GS dump replayed while a
GLES client at high EGL priority draws 120 times a second: the replay
differed from the sysmem reference in 47 to 71 of 80 frames with the
BANDWIDTH + TUNE_SMALL default and 7 to 25 with TU_DEBUG=gmem; with this
change, 0 in both. An experiment build counted 23 to 44 runs of a
switch-back amble per replay and none of the bin restore preamble.

Ported by hand to Mesa 7a1fc756809 for XDroid360 from bmdhacks/armsx2-turnip
267e559 (Brian Degenhardt, MIT): raw CP_MEM_TO_REG packets instead of
cs->mem_to_reg, and store_3d_blit restores RB_BUFFER_CNTL with
CP_SCRATCH_TO_REG here, so its copy is saved to a fourth slot and
copied back with CP_MEM_TO_MEM (the value is not known when recording). TU_DEBUG=nopreemptrestore turns it off (read at
device creation), for A/B on one build.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc
